"guard.how.relay.title" = "A relay at the proxy's address";
"guard.how.relay" = "The pages of a profile with a SOCKS5 proxy get one server for WebRTC — a relay (TURN) on 127.0.0.1 inside Lumen. It sends their UDP through the proxy's UDP ASSOCIATE, so sites and peers see the proxy's address. Pages get no candidate with this Mac's addresses.";
"guard.how.guard.title" = "The network guard";
"guard.how.guard" = "Lumen's system extension is a content filter. It carries and reads nothing — it isn't even allowed to open a connection: it only lets a connection through or drops it. The process of a profile whose WebRTC goes through its proxy, and whatever WebKit and macOS open for it, may connect only to its proxy and to this Mac (127.0.0.1); everything else is dropped. Other apps' connections, and Lumen's own — updates, the account, sync — are let through at once.";
"guard.how.limits.title" = "Limits";
"guard.how.limits" = "It needs a SOCKS5 proxy whose UDP ASSOCIATE works: this is checked before the profile starts, and without UDP WebRTC is off in the profile. An HTTP proxy cannot carry UDP. The relay carries UDP only: WebRTC over TCP (TURN/TCP) is not supported. To know a profile's connections, the filter sees the start of every new connection of this Mac — its address and app; none of it is recorded or sent anywhere.";
"guard.state.proving" = "Being checked on this Mac…";
"guard.todo.proving" = "Lumen checks that the guard sees the connections WebKit opens for a profile: a helper process with no profile's data sends one WebRTC request to an address that leads nowhere, and the guard must drop it. About 10 seconds.";
"guard.todo.proofFailed" = "The check failed: the guard did not see the connection WebKit opened for a profile — it would have nothing to hold the profile to its proxy with. So WebRTC is off in profiles with a proxy. Click Check Again; after an update of macOS or Safari the check runs again by itself.";
"guardNotice.restartNeeded" = "The network guard starts working after you restart this Mac: macOS finishes installing it at startup. Until then WebRTC is off in profiles with a proxy.";
